1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:02,280
I will extract the evidence from him.

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:03,640
There's a way to do it...

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:08,880
Watch out!

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,320
We found two types of glucose inhibitors
in his blood.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,640
Someone must have drugged him.

6
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,400
And you suspect me?

7
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,680
You think she's your friend?

8
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:30,720
Don't forgot how Ben died.

9
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,320
Don't you feel guilty when you see her?

10
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:45,320
If someone inadvertently
spilled the beans about something,

11
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,680
what would happen?

12
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:50,800
Ask yourself how I treated you.

13
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:53,400
You're very good to me...

14
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,440
You gave me food and shelter

15
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:56,760
and took good care of me.

16
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:00,080
I went to jail and my money was confiscated.

17
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:02,400
I only want what is rightfully mine.

18
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,920
Won't you help me?

19
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,600
Of course...

20
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,080
Good girl!

21
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,840
Ben had two women in his life.

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,160
If the mistress doesn't have the money,

23
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,640
the wife must have it.

24
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:16,480
Go talk to the wife in the hospital.

25
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,400
I will.

26
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:24,280
Mary, let me help you.

27
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,600
Hi, I'm Cathy's friend.

28
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,360
Suet?

29
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,000
Out! Get the hell out!

30
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,360
Get out! You...

31
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:36,560
What are you doing here?

32
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:37,600
I was going to help her pick that up...

33
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,280
Get out!

34
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,200
Just go!

35
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,920
Is that necessary?
Just go.

36
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,400
How can you be friends with her?

37
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,800
She's with those thugs who killed Ben.

38
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,480
She's a baddie.

39
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,880
She called me Mary.

40
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,560
You told her about me?

41
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:57,040
No. I'm friends with her because of Ben.

42
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,240
Precisely because of Ben,

43
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,160
you should stay away from her.

44
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,840
Calm down. Don't get so agitated.

45
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,440
What are you doing here?

46
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:10,480
I meant to have lunch with you

47
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:11,600
and you didn't call me back.

48
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,120
That's why I came over.

49
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,400
Mary doesn't want you to contact me.

50
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,760
She has no right to choose your friends.

51
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,000
You shouldn't come here.

52
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,640
I'm really busy today.

53
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:23,720
You should leave.

54
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:31,000
Are you better?

55
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:36,640
Better find out where the money is.

56
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,720
Cathy, you're back!

57
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:42,160
Are you tired?

58
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:45,040
I made soup. I'll heat it up for you.

59
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:50,400
Sorry, I didn't expect Mary to react
like that when she saw me.

60
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,280
I didn't mean it.

61
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,640
You know I don't use my head.

62
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,480
Please don't be mad.

63
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:04,280
I have good news.

64
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:05,720
My tutor at the hairstyling school

65
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,320
wants to recommend me to study
styling in Seoul.

66
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,160
Let's go together.

67
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:12,000
I can't get away.

68
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,480
You don't have money?

69
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:16,960
Thanks.

70
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,640
Thank you.
Thanks.

71
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,480
Did you leave me the keycard?

72
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,160
Yes, it's for you.

73
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:33,920
Is this about the legal loopholes?

74
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,720
Don't ask. Just keep it for me.

75
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:41,280
But we're still tracking down the $1.8M

76
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:43,360
Lau Yue-bun received for money laundering.

77
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:46,840
The money should be handed in to the Police.

78
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:50,160
But you risked your life for it.

79
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,160
I know what to do.

80
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,280
I will spend it on Mary.

81
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:59,040
I can't leave even if I have the money.

82
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,840
Why not, if money is not the issue?

83
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,960
I can't just drop everything.

84
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,440
Because of Mary?

85
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:10,320
Is it worth it?

86
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,080
You intend to spend the rest of
your life like this?

87
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,640
Give up your life and your dream?

88
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,640
My dream is to be a nurse.

89
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,960
I know you're a good person.

90
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,840
But don't you think this is too much?

91
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,400
Do you really want to do this?

92
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:23,840
Or only because of Ben?

93
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,920
It's one thing if he gave you money.

94
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:30,640
If he didn't, how can you take on
the burden of a patient forever?

95
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,720
You're still young, you don't understand.

96
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:35,520
I'm tired. I'll go shower.

97
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,080
What happened all of a sudden?

98
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,360
Did you call Dr. Chung?

99
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,720
Yes, he's on his way.

100
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:47,640
It's a relapse of her GBS,
Guillain- Barre Syndrome.

101
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,080
She was making good progress this week.

102
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,360
Why did this happen so suddenly?

103
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:52,720
That's the nature of GBS.

104
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,640
Her condition is now stabilized

105
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,520
and she's out of danger.

106
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:58,000
But the relapse affected her
respiratory muscles.

107
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,960
She'll have trouble breathing
and heart arrhythmia.

108
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:03,520
Should we give her IVIG like last time?

109
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,600
IVIG is the most effective treatment.

110
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:07,080
But it's expensive.

111
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,200
Do it. Money is not an issue.

112
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:14,160
She authorized me to make decisions for her,

113
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,920
to use whatever means to treat her.

114
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,200
OK, I'll set it up.

115
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:17,920
Thanks.

116
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,400
Ben risked his life for the money.

117
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,040
For him, you must hang in there.

118
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,520
You're late? More OT?

119
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,280
I'll reheat the food for you.

120
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,080
No need. I'll just grab something,

121
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:41,200
take a shower and go back to the hospital.

122
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,800
Why are you so busy?

123
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,880
Her condition took a turn for the worse.

124
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,160
I want to be with her.

125
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,200
The next few days are crucial.

126
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:53,840
If Mary is in trouble, she'll get the money.

127
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:57,280
If I follow her, I'll find the money.

128
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,640
This is where she keeps Ben's money!

129
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,360
Where the hell are you? Get over here.

130
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,400
I told you to look for the money.

131
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:17,360
Did you find it?

132
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,880
I have not seen her with any money.

133
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,640
Maybe she spent it already.

134
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:24,400
Use your head. She spent $1.8M?!

135
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,320
That broad must have it.

136
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:29,080
But I looked everywhere. There is nothing.

137
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,400
You don't want to help me, right?

138
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:35,040
Of course not!

139
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,080
If you don't want to help me,

140
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:40,160
I have other ways to make her cough it up.

141
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:42,880
I have another plan to make her talk.

142
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,720
Let me try.

143
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,600
He doesn't seem to believe me.

144
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:50,240
Can't let him know where Cathy lives.

145
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:52,400
Even if your friend wants someone
to share the flat,

146
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:53,960
you don't need to leave in such a hurry.

147
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:56,080
If I don't hurry,
what if she found someone else?

148
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,120
I'd miss a good deal.

149
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,160
Male or female?

150
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,600
Girlfriend.

151
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,200
Let's catch a taxi over there.

152
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:12,240
Cathy, are you OK?

153
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,600
Did you send someone to run us over?

154
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:18,480
Yes.

155
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:23,760
I told you I have another plan.

156
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,760
What plan? Let's hear it.

157
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,160
I was thinking...

158
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,520
Stop jerking me around.

159
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,680
You won't tell me where the broad lives

160
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:32,720
because you don't want me to find her.

161
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,240
You think I don't know?

162
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,480
You claimed to have a plan,

163
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,400
then you ghosted me.

164
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,720
You want the money for yourself
and then skip town, right?

165
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:45,440
No! I really looked everywhere
but didn't find the money.

166
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:47,760
Are you trying to help the broad?

167
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:51,840
You took me in and gave me money.

168
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,800
I know you're the good guy.

169
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,600
Cathy is in worse shape than I am.

170
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,800
The dude is dead,

171
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:59,280
and she's stuck with the invalid wife.

172
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:03,440
You think I'm a moron like Dummy and Shek?

173
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:05,520
You had their heads spinning
just by talking to them.

174
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:07,600
Listen, I let you hang around,

175
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,360
only because I need you to help
them let off steam,

176
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:10,400
so those morons would do my bidding.

177
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,520
Now that you're useless to me,

178
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:12,560
I'm going to make you a whore.

179
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,000
Come here...

180
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:17,200
Listen, if I could kill Ben,

181
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,160
I can certainly kill you.

182
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,600
If you won't tell me where the money is,

183
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:22,800
you're not leaving, do you hear me?

184
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:02,240
Why are you calling me so late?

185
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:04,160
Cathy, help me!

186
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,880
Go! Drive!
OK!

187
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:28,720
What happened? How did you get roughed up?

188
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:32,000
I'm sorry, Cathy.

189
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:36,720
There's something I haven't told you...

190
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,080
I'm in contact with Brother Kin.

191
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:42,880
You said you wanted to live a normal life.

192
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,480
Why do you want to stick with him?

193
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,880
I thought he was good to me.

194
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,600
That's why I listen to him.

195
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:53,200
But he was using me the whole time.

196
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:58,000
He rammed my head against the wall

197
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:00,400
just like he did when he killed Ben.

198
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:02,920
What? He killed Ben?

199
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:05,600
What exactly happened?

200
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,200
You must tell me the whole story.

201
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:09,760
Ben came to see Brother Kin.

202
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:13,760
As usual, I was sleeping
with my headphones on.

203
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:16,160
Then the battery of my phone died,

204
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:18,000
and I heard a racket downstairs.

205
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,600
I went down to check it out.

206
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:31,800
Stop staring. Give me a hand.

207
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:33,360
What?

208
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,040
Lift his legs.

209
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:47,440
Go back up.

210
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:50,400
Lie down.

211
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,800
Put the headphones back on.

212
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:56,240
Remember, we were asleep the whole time.

213
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:57,440
We never went downstairs

214
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:59,040
and didn't know what happened, OK?

215
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,960
My mind went blank.

216
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,800
Brother Kin told me to pretend
I didn't know anything.

217
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:06,640
I really didn't want to know.

218
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:13,280
There's a lot of blood. He's...dead!

219
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,920
Brother Kin...get up!

220
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,320
Brother Kin, we're screwed...

221
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,320
Get up...don't sleep anymore.
Get up!

222
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:20,000
Brother Kin...

223
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,000
What's wrong?

224
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,800
We killed Ben.

225
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,800
Stay here. I'll go look.

226
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:28,480
Hurry...
Come on...

227
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:31,760
I didn't go down and thought I'd be OK.

228
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:34,880
Brother Kin, the air con is on high.

229
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,360
We sprayed loads of air freshener.

230
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:39,520
People won't smell the body so quickly.

231
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,280
Brother Kin, I had nothing to do with this.

232
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,040
Do I have to go on the run?

233
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,720
You watched while it happened

234
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:48,240
and you moved Ben's body.

235
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,200
What do you think?

236
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,360
It's too late to back out now.

237
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,640
Just go!

238
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,920
There's a citywide manhunt for us.

239
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,360
We can't stay in hiding much longer.

240
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:06,240
Those two morons thought they did it anyway.

241
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:08,880
Just pin it on them.

242
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:10,800
What do you have in mind?

243
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:15,040
I want you to sneak out, go to the Police

244
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,560
and rat on them.

245
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,720
What? Are you sure?

246
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:22,000
I'm wanted by the Police too.

247
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,760
Would they believe me?

248
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,200
Don't worry,

249
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:28,720
we can all prove we were sleeping upstairs

250
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,240
and didn't know what happened.

251
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,680
They're bound to ask you who
solicited to commit murder.

252
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,520
Tell them I did,

253
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,760
but you heard me telling them the next day

254
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:40,080
that I was only kidding. Remember that!

255
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:45,680
I knew it wasn't that simple.

256
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,520
Tai Yat-kin was not only the instigator,

257
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,880
he was also the killer.

258
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:50,160
I need to call the Police.

259
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:53,120
No, you can't.

260
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,960
I perjured myself,

261
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,040
the cops would arrest me too.

262
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,520
Then why did you cover up for him?

263
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,680
I didn't know any better then.

264
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:04,960
I thought he was the good guy and
wouldn't hurt me.

265
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,560
But it was only after I met you,

266
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:09,120
I realized what a good person is like.

267
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,600
After Brother Kin got out of jail,

268
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,760
I didn't want him to contact me.

269
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:19,360
But he insisted you kept Ben's money.

270
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,280
He wouldn't leave me alone

271
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:23,600
and forced me to find out from you
where the money was.

272
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:27,840
I knew you kept the money
in the mini storage.

273
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,760
But I didn't tell him.

274
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:34,800
Because I know you need the money
for Mary's treatment.

275
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,760
At least you came to your senses

276
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:39,600
and didn't tell him everything.

277
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,520
I didn't want him to follow me

278
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:43,680
because I didn't want him to know
where you live.

279
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,840
That's why I moved out.

280
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,840
But he still found me...

281
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:51,040
You're saying he sent someone
to run us over?

282
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:54,720
Yes! Don't go to the Police!

283
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:56,560
He's crazy.

284
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:00,240
Besides, Ben's money is illegal.

285
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:03,440
You can't tell the Police.

286
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:07,040
I will extract the evidence from him.

287
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:10,400
How? I can't go back to him.

288
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,400
There's a way to do it...

289
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,840
But it'll be too risky for you.

290
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:22,800
No, I shouldn't have ideas like that.

291
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,560
It's too risky. I can't let you do it.

292
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:26,320
You want to nail him?

293
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,840
OK, if you want to nail him,

294
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:32,400
let's nail this creep. I'll help you.

295
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:34,480
Just tell me what to do.

296
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:38,000
I told you to watch her. What happened?

297
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,880
I remember I forgot to buy smokes for you.

298
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,080
You need two people to do that?

299
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:44,880
Brother Kin, I finally found out.

300
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,160
About time you showed up.

301
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:50,080
Don't get upset.

302
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,360
I have something to tell you.

303
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,760
I ran away because I suddenly remember

304
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:56,000
a few days ago, Cathy was sneaking around

305
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:59,040
doing something under the stove
in the kitchen.

306
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:01,200
I was wondering if that's where
she kept the money.

307
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,200
I know she worked the late shift last night,

308
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:06,960
so I hurried home and I found the money.

309
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,640
I brought it to you right away.

310
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:12,080
I had to lean on you to get anything done.

311
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:14,400
I saw cops around when I was coming here.

312
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,720
I was afraid they'd stop me but they didn't.

313
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,600
Where's the rest?

314
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:22,480
That's all I found. Keep it in a safe place.

315
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,120
I'm hungry.

316
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,720
Go get something to eat.

317
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:30,000
Look at all the beer. Let's have a drink

318
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:32,000
to celebrate finding the money.

319
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:37,600
Come on...

320
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:46,080
Don't be vicious like last time,

321
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:47,560
you had me scared.

322
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:49,680
You threatened to make me a whore.

323
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,600
Were you joking?

324
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:55,560
You saw me when I'm pissed off.

325
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,800
Don't get on my bad side.

326
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:01,800
When you said "If I could kill Ben,
I can certainly kill you",

327
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,440
were you kidding?

328
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:05,440
Brother Kin is good for his words.

329
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:06,960
You're such a bragger.

330
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:08,480
I bet Ben went crazy last time

331
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:09,920
and it was self-defense.

332
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,960
That weasel Ben deserved to die.

333
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:19,680
Hey, Ben...

334
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:22,640
Open the safe and get me the money.

335
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:24,880
No, what can you do about it?

336
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:38,640
I saw the nail on the wall

337
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:39,920
and I rammed his head right into it.

338
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,800
Those two morons thought they killed him

339
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:54,960
and took the rap.

340
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:56,400
Let's not talk about that.

341
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,360
Have another one.

342
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:08,240
Bloody hell, you made a recording?

343
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,680
You think you'll get me talking?

344
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:14,880
(Suet)

345
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,160
Hello, Suet?

346
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:20,960
That bloody recording pen won't
send me to jail.

347
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,000
Help me...Let me out...

348
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:24,640
You want her back? Bring the money.

349
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:27,680
Don't call the Police or she's dead.
Help...

350
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,520
OK...I'll give it to you.

351
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:31,440
Do not hurt her, you hear me?

352
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:58,880
Watch it. It's dangerous to drink and drive.

353
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,520
Shut up.

354
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,640
I'm dead if I don't have the money.

355
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,200
Well?

356
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:27,360
You want to play games? Where's the rest?

357
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:29,120
I used some of it.

358
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,720
This is all I have left.

359
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,520
You can take the money,

360
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:35,080
but I get the girl.

361
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:36,960
You'll get her when you give me the rest.

362
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:37,680
Hey...

363
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,320
Get in...

364
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:56,640
Hey!

365
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,200
Watch out!

366
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:04,000
Suet...

367
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:08,560
Wake up...

368
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:35,560
The victim Tai Yat-kin is certified.

369
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:50,480
That weasel Ben deserved to die.

370
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:52,160
I saw the nail on the wall

371
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:53,560
and I rammed his head right into it.

372
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:55,760
Those two morons thought they killed him

373
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:57,920
and took the rap.

374
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:01,360
Luckily, you had two recording pens

375
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:03,680
and managed to record
Tai Yat-kin's confession.

376
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:05,760
It was Suet's idea.

377
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:07,280
I didn't know beforehand.

378
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:09,920
We still don't recommend taking such risks.

379
00:22:10,080 --> 00:22:11,600
You're lucky you got away,

380
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:13,360
next time, you could be dead.

381
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:14,880
I know.

382
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:17,320
Maybe this is his retribution.

383
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:18,400
At first, I was worried

384
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:19,760
even if we had incriminating evidence,

385
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,520
we may not be able to convict him.

386
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,600
Gogo Sir, you said one cannot be charged
with the same offense twice.

387
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:28,720
Maybe a killer should pay with his life.

388
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,840
At least justice is served for Ben.

389
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,560
The long arm of the law will get you.

390
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:39,600
One more thing...though the money
went up in smoke with the car,

391
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:40,960
but according to procedures,

392
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:43,040
you must declare the amount.

393
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:48,000
It's around $300K, that's my entire savings.

394
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:50,560
What a shame it went up in smoke!

395
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:54,120
No, at least nobody is hurt.

396
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:02,520
You were just getting better.

397
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:04,000
I'm sorry I had to transfer you.

398
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:06,400
Don't be. You can look after me.

399
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:08,120
It's the least I could do.

400
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,400
Gogo Sir was right.

401
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:14,600
You could have died, all because of me.

402
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:17,560
Still, I volunteered to do it.

403
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:19,880
As long as you got your wish.

404
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,120
Thank you.

405
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:26,960
You won't need to live in fear anymore.

406
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:33,080
Cathy, I made so many mistakes in the past,

407
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:35,040
I hope you can forgive me

408
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:36,560
and accept me as your friend.

409
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:40,400
Don't be silly. We're friends already.

410
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:43,200
Let's move on, OK?

411
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:44,280
Yes!

412
00:23:47,080 --> 00:23:49,120
Dr. Chung said your treatment
is very effective.

413
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:51,120
He's confident you'll make more progress.

414
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,720
You may recover.

415
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:53,880
Really?

416
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:56,280
Thanks so much for taking such risks

417
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:58,360
and kept Ben's money to save me.

418
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:00,720
And you avenged him.

419
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,880
I think we have Suet to thank.

420
00:24:05,040 --> 00:24:07,360
I didn't expect her to take such risks.

421
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,440
I guess I was wrong about her.

422
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:11,600
I was biased against her at first.

423
00:24:11,760 --> 00:24:16,720
She's actually just a kid longing for
someone to care about her

424
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:19,880
and be nice to her.

425
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,920
Cathy, what are you doing?

426
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:38,320
The bag was dirty,

427
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:40,160
I was going to empty it out and wash it.

428
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:43,080
No, I can manage.

429
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:47,360
Speaking like a true professional,

430
00:24:47,440 --> 00:24:49,040
who doesn't want anyone to touch your tools.

431
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:52,640
You usually sleep like a log,

432
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:53,760
and very hard to wake you up.

433
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:55,280
How come you woke up so easily just now?

434
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:59,880
I don't know. Maybe I slept too much
in the hospital.

435
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:02,640
Besides, so much happened lately,

436
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:04,400
I still feel jittery.

437
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,640
I have the day off today.

438
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:08,840
Let's go out and relax?

439
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:10,080
Great!

440
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:11,360
Where do you want to go?

441
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:19,600
Looks like you want to go to the beach.

442
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:22,360
Yes, I know it's childish, but fun.

443
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:24,080
I also want to take loads of pictures.

444
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:25,280
OK!

445
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:29,920
Hello?

446
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:38,000
OK, I'll come in. Bye!

447
00:25:38,440 --> 00:25:39,560
What is it?

448
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:42,000
Sorry, a colleague is sick

449
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:44,320
and they need me to fill in a shift.

450
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:46,280
It's OK. Go to work.

451
00:25:46,360 --> 00:25:47,440
We'll do this next time.

452
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:59,120
Crash...I found it.

453
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:06,280
You're alone? Where's your family?

454
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:09,920
My wife is at home.

455
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:13,440
My kids are working.

456
00:26:13,640 --> 00:26:15,280
You have kids?

457
00:26:16,040 --> 00:26:17,440
Who came with you?

458
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:20,880
Chi...there you are!

459
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,840
I was looking for you. Let's go.

460
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:23,920
You're his wife?

461
00:26:24,080 --> 00:26:26,880
No, I work for his family.

462
00:26:27,040 --> 00:26:28,520
You shouldn't be running around.

463
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:30,640
Your wife is waiting at the door. Come on...

464
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:33,200
Does he really have kids?

465
00:26:33,320 --> 00:26:36,160
Yes, Chi is a happy man!

466
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:37,840
Let's go...say goodbye!

467
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,200
Come on...

468
00:26:44,880 --> 00:26:48,120
Miss Tse, we have questions for you.

469
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:51,800
What are glucose inhibitors for?

470
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:56,360
They help diabetics control their
blood sugar level.

471
00:26:56,520 --> 00:26:58,600
What happens if you take an overdose?

472
00:26:58,880 --> 00:27:01,040
You'll have low blood sugar level,

473
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:04,480
general fatigue, dizziness, blurry vision.

474
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:06,960
In serious cases, you'll go into
hypoglycemic shock.

475
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:11,320
Why do you ask?

476
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:15,200
We suspect Tai Yat-kin's death
was not an accident.

477
00:27:16,360 --> 00:27:17,920
Forensics examined the car.

478
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:20,080
There was no sign of mechanical failure.

479
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:22,120
But his autopsy report showed

480
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:25,680
a high dosage of glucose inhibitor
in his blood.

481
00:27:25,840 --> 00:27:29,080
We suspect the low blood sugar level
made him unconscious

482
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:30,520
and he lost control of the car.

483
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:34,280
Hold on...Suet told me

484
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:36,400
Tai Yat-kin drank heavily the night before.

485
00:27:36,560 --> 00:27:38,400
Alcohol can increase the drug effect

486
00:27:38,520 --> 00:27:42,360
which may cause hypoglycemic shock.

487
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:47,920
Or after the intake of alcohol,

488
00:27:48,040 --> 00:27:50,040
he overdosed on the drugs.

489
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:53,360
Situations like that happened before
to other patients.

490
00:27:53,520 --> 00:27:54,560
Neither is possible.

491
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:58,360
We found two types of
glucose inhibitors in his blood.

492
00:27:58,440 --> 00:27:59,920
There was no record of him
switching his meds.

493
00:28:00,080 --> 00:28:04,360
We also found a bottle of
oolong tea in the car

494
00:28:04,440 --> 00:28:06,640
that contained one of the
glucose inhibitors.

495
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:08,560
We're quite certain he was drugged.

496
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,200
This person knows Tai Yat-kin well

497
00:28:11,360 --> 00:28:12,880
and that he was diabetic.

498
00:28:13,080 --> 00:28:14,480
This person was smart enough

499
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:18,480
to use a glucose inhibitor
to cause an accident

500
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:20,120
to cover up the murder.

501
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:22,880
How can ordinary people get the drugs?

502
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:26,080
Maybe someone who works in a hospital?

503
00:28:26,680 --> 00:28:28,360
And you suspect me?

504
00:28:31,640 --> 00:28:34,720
Suet, if you don't start rinsing,

505
00:28:34,800 --> 00:28:36,320
you won't finish in time

506
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:37,920
and the tutor will dock your score.

507
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:48,640
Blood! Blood!

508
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:51,440
And you suspect me?

509
00:28:51,520 --> 00:28:53,640
Tai Yat-kin killed the love of your life.

510
00:28:53,760 --> 00:28:55,120
You must have hated him.

511
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:57,320
That's your motive.

512
00:28:57,400 --> 00:29:00,800
As a nurse, you have easy access
to the drugs.

513
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:03,560
You can get drugs elsewhere.

514
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:05,520
A lot of drug stores out there

515
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:07,520
will sell you this sort of drugs.

516
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:10,520
You said it yourself, I'm a nurse,

517
00:29:10,640 --> 00:29:13,520
I'm unlikely to mix up the drugs.

518
00:29:13,600 --> 00:29:16,040
That's why we suspect someone else.

519
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:17,600
Who else is there?

520
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:20,760
Who else has a motive,

521
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:22,840
knows Tai Yat-kin well

522
00:29:22,960 --> 00:29:25,880
and has the chance to do it?

523
00:29:26,080 --> 00:29:27,680
You suspect Suet?

524
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:29,840
She's the prime suspect.

525
00:29:29,920 --> 00:29:31,520
But we have no proof.

526
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:33,120
That's why we came to ask you

527
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:35,560
if you noticed anything odd about her.

528
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:39,760
Did she ask you about glucose
inhibitors beforehand?

529
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:41,040
No.

530
00:29:41,800 --> 00:29:44,160
I didn't notice anything odd about her.

531
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:47,600
She also didn't ask me anything about drugs.

532
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:50,360
She was browsing online that morning.

533
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:52,760
Was she checking on glucose inhibitors?

534
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:55,120
When she bought the recording pen,

535
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:56,560
she said she needed to get something else.

536
00:29:56,680 --> 00:29:58,160
She bought oolong tea.

537
00:29:58,680 --> 00:30:02,320
Tai Yat-kin was drinking oolong tea.

538
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:05,200
She spiked the oolong tea?

539
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:06,880
I need to get money from the mini storage.

540
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:08,120
I won't go with you.

541
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,520
I still have errands to run.

542
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:10,880
OK. I'll go this way.

543
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:12,000
I go that way.
See you at home.

544
00:30:12,080 --> 00:30:15,920
Did Suet pick up the glucose inhibitor
from the drug store after that?

545
00:30:17,240 --> 00:30:18,880
I shouldn't say that.

546
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:20,760
What if I was overthinking?

547
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,040
(Pharmacist's Tip...Avoid drinking alcohol)

548
00:30:25,120 --> 00:30:26,000
(Alcohol can increase the
drug's side effects...)

549
00:30:26,080 --> 00:30:26,800
(and may cause low blood sugar)

550
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:28,600
Did she kill him?

551
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:31,840
Luckily, you had two recording pens

552
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:34,160
and managed to record
Tai Yat-kin's confession.

553
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:36,320
It was Suet's idea.

554
00:30:36,640 --> 00:30:38,800
She bought an extra recording pen

555
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:40,880
because she had another plan?

556
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:43,040
She wanted Tai Yat-kin dead from the start?

557
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:45,680
Why did she do it?

558
00:30:46,080 --> 00:30:48,280
Since we already have the evidence,

559
00:30:48,400 --> 00:30:50,520
why must Tai Yat-kin die?

560
00:30:50,600 --> 00:30:51,640
I need to call the Police.

561
00:30:51,760 --> 00:30:54,520
No, you can't.

562
00:30:54,680 --> 00:30:56,160
I perjured myself,

563
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:58,400
the cops would arrest me too.

564
00:30:58,560 --> 00:31:00,880
Was she worried if Tai Yat-kin went to jail,

565
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:03,600
she'll be exposed of perjury?

566
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:04,760
Was she scared?

567
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:07,320
But she really could have died.

568
00:31:07,440 --> 00:31:08,360
Was it worth it?

569
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:11,120
What's her reason?

570
00:31:13,280 --> 00:31:14,480
Have another one.

571
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:15,840
You made a recording?

572
00:31:17,280 --> 00:31:18,960
You think you'll get me talking?

573
00:31:19,720 --> 00:31:22,760
Stop hitting me. Check the recording pen.

574
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:24,160
There are no batteries.

575
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:25,600
The broad wanted me to get evidence.

576
00:31:25,680 --> 00:31:28,080
I bought the recording pen to humor her.

577
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:30,400
What now?

578
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:32,480
You were thinking of a way

579
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:34,840
to make the broad cough up the money.

580
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,520
Call her now.

581
00:31:36,600 --> 00:31:38,720
Tell her you saw through our plan.

582
00:31:38,840 --> 00:31:40,280
Pretend you kidnapped me

583
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:42,120
and tell her to pay a ransom.

584
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:44,560
If she refused, tell her you'll kill me.

585
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:48,040
She trusts me, she'll pay the ransom.

586
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,000
Let's try that.

587
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:10,560
It's a kidnapping. I need to tie you up.

588
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:13,040
The whole nine yards.

589
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:22,640
These are the messages between Ben and me.

590
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:25,200
When did she get ahold of my phone?

591
00:32:27,760 --> 00:32:31,200
Wait...these messages are transposed.

592
00:32:31,880 --> 00:32:34,160
These are messages from Ben's phone.

593
00:32:34,800 --> 00:32:36,640
Did Suet have Ben's phone?

594
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:38,160
Cathy, what are you doing?

595
00:32:39,320 --> 00:32:40,480
The bag was dirty,

596
00:32:40,560 --> 00:32:42,400
I was going to empty it out and wash it.

597
00:32:42,560 --> 00:32:45,280
No, I can manage.

598
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:30,960
It's OK...don't let Cathy spot anything.

599
00:33:38,040 --> 00:33:43,880
Cathy...you have the afternoon off tomorrow?

600
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:44,880
Yes!

601
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,760
Let's go to the beach.

602
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:48,400
We didn't get to go last time.

603
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:51,280
Great! Which one?

604
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:52,400
I'll let you decide.

605
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:57,040
I'm almost there. Are you off yet?

606
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:01,680
(Ko Sir calling)

607
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,000
You didn't text me back.

608
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:08,840
I was afraid you had to work OT

609
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:10,200
and blow me off again.

610
00:34:38,600 --> 00:34:41,160
I will work very hard to make a lot of money

611
00:34:41,240 --> 00:34:43,520
and buy the prettiest and biggest castle

612
00:34:43,600 --> 00:34:45,200
so you and I can move in together.

613
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:48,760
I had fun building a castle today.

614
00:34:48,880 --> 00:34:50,800
Today is the happiest day of my life.

615
00:34:52,200 --> 00:34:55,160
You're too old for a fantasy, silly.

616
00:34:56,840 --> 00:34:59,920
This is fun, but this is made of sand.

617
00:35:00,080 --> 00:35:04,000
It'll be washed away
and you'll have nothing left.

618
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:08,760
If I can't have it,
it's nice to just look at it.

619
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:11,440
When the next wave moves in,
there's nothing to look at.

620
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,840
Haven't you heard? You won't leave
a trace in the water,

621
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:16,960
But life is different.

622
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:19,760
If you did something,

623
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:24,240
you'll leave traces, however small they are,

624
00:35:26,880 --> 00:35:28,240
people will always find out.

625
00:35:34,240 --> 00:35:36,000
Did you find out something?

626
00:35:36,120 --> 00:35:38,880
Though I don't entirely know why you did it.

627
00:35:39,280 --> 00:35:41,120
It broke my heart just the same.

628
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:45,920
But one must bear the consequence
of one's mistakes.

629
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:52,320
Miss Ho Pui-suet,

630
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:54,720
you're suspected of murdering Tai Yat-kin.

631
00:35:54,800 --> 00:35:57,160
Please come with us.

632
00:35:58,520 --> 00:35:59,920
You called them?

633
00:36:00,080 --> 00:36:01,240
I did not.

634
00:36:02,120 --> 00:36:04,000
You're someone dearest to me.

635
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:05,920
But you betrayed me!

636
00:36:07,600 --> 00:36:08,960
You said you have forgiven me

637
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:11,200
and treated me as your best friend.

638
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:13,840
It was a lie, wasn't it?

639
00:36:14,840 --> 00:36:20,000
Why did you do it? Why? Why?

640
00:36:20,120 --> 00:36:21,720
I did not.

641
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:26,480
I never intended to hurt you.

642
00:36:26,560 --> 00:36:28,880
Save it.

643
00:36:30,040 --> 00:36:31,840
I don't want to listen to you.

644
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,280
Miss Ho, please calm down.

645
00:36:33,440 --> 00:36:35,600
Miss Tse didn't call us.

646
00:36:35,720 --> 00:36:37,360
We were unable to contact her

647
00:36:37,480 --> 00:36:38,880
and we suspect she was covering up for you.

648
00:36:39,040 --> 00:36:40,160
We looked for her in the hospital

649
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:42,760
and found out you might be here.

650
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:47,840
I'm sorry...

651
00:36:47,960 --> 00:36:50,560
I intended to persuade you
to turn yourself in.

652
00:36:50,760 --> 00:36:54,240
Sorry, I should have told you.

653
00:36:59,560 --> 00:37:02,120
Thanks for coming with me today.

654
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:04,240
I'll always remember today.

655
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:33,440
Baby, can you have breakfast
with me tomorrow?

656
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,040
Why can't we have dinner together?

657
00:37:35,240 --> 00:37:37,040
Why are you fixated on breakfast?

658
00:37:37,560 --> 00:37:40,480
Because breakfast is the
happiest time of the day.

659
00:37:40,600 --> 00:37:42,320
Having someone to eat breakfast with

660
00:37:42,480 --> 00:37:44,240
is happier than happy.

661
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:47,440
I didn't know you're a breakfast person.

662
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:49,440
I don't usually get up this early.

663
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:50,760
But I want to be with you.

664
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:52,880
I think eating breakfast with someone

665
00:37:53,040 --> 00:37:54,320
is a very happy thing.

666
00:37:54,680 --> 00:37:56,320
Pictures from an instant camera

667
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:57,760
have a different feeling.

668
00:37:58,480 --> 00:38:00,400
I like the surprise.

669
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:03,760
You'll never know what you captured.

670
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:06,000
Why would someone young like you
like something so old fashioned?

671
00:38:06,160 --> 00:38:08,480
Age has nothing to do with it.

672
00:38:08,560 --> 00:38:10,800
You never know what you captured.

673
00:38:10,920 --> 00:38:12,400
I like the surprise.

674
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:14,480
The adult world is so exhausting.

675
00:38:14,640 --> 00:38:17,040
Let's do something stupid

676
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:18,800
and play with the sand on the beach.

677
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:20,560
Looks like you want to go to the beach.

678
00:38:20,720 --> 00:38:23,440
Yes, I know it's childish, but fun.

679
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:26,400
I will work very hard to make a lot of money

680
00:38:26,520 --> 00:38:28,640
and buy the prettiest and biggest castle

681
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:30,320
so you and I can move in together.

682
00:38:31,440 --> 00:38:34,200
If I can't have it,
it's nice to just look at it.

683
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:38,400
Cathy is honest and kind.

684
00:38:38,560 --> 00:38:41,440
She can't bear to have a friend
who was a murderer.

685
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:45,840
Ho Pui-suet, you are charged with
the murder of Tai Yat-kin.

686
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:47,240
How do you plead?

687
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:53,920
Guilty.

688
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:56,320
Why did you kill the victim?

689
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:05,280
Listen, whoever stands between
me and my money,

690
00:39:05,360 --> 00:39:06,560
I don't care if it's the chick inside,

691
00:39:06,640 --> 00:39:07,760
or the nurse out there.

692
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:09,160
I'll kill them both.

693
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:11,360
I was afraid if Tai Yat-kin was arrested,

694
00:39:11,520 --> 00:39:13,200
the whole thing will come to light.

695
00:39:13,800 --> 00:39:16,320
He'd say I committed perjury
to protect him.

696
00:39:17,080 --> 00:39:18,720
I didn't want to go to jail.

697
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:21,520
Tai Yat-kin was a lunatic.

698
00:39:21,720 --> 00:39:24,000
He told me if I didn't do as he said,

699
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:27,280
he'd get someone to rape me and kill me.

700
00:39:27,400 --> 00:39:29,160
I had to protect myself.

701
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:31,520
Compared to yourself,

702
00:39:31,720 --> 00:39:34,480
you're even more afraid of him hurting me.

703
00:39:35,200 --> 00:39:36,720
It wasn't self-protection.

704
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:38,960
You were protecting me.

705
00:39:39,040 --> 00:39:42,000
I was scared. I feared him.

706
00:39:42,120 --> 00:39:45,200
He went too far and made me do it.

707
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:47,360
If you want to nail him,

708
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:50,400
let's nail this creep. I'll help you.

709
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:52,800
Just tell me what to do.

710
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:54,400
You didn't do it for yourself.

711
00:39:54,520 --> 00:39:57,040
Everything you did, you did it for me.

712
00:39:57,520 --> 00:39:59,440
For me, no matter how scared you were,

713
00:39:59,560 --> 00:40:02,000
you went ahead and did it
with no second thoughts.

714
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:06,480
To be able to do one thing
for someone I love,

715
00:40:06,560 --> 00:40:08,400
I have no regrets.

716
00:40:20,280 --> 00:40:23,160
Next time, let's target for
the outlying islands.

717
00:40:24,040 --> 00:40:26,960
OK! You're recovering so well.

718
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:28,800
I think it'll happen soon.

719
00:40:32,120 --> 00:40:34,120
What about you?

720
00:40:34,520 --> 00:40:35,760
I saw on the news,

721
00:40:35,880 --> 00:40:37,440
Suet pleaded guilty in court.

722
00:40:38,560 --> 00:40:40,800
I don't quite understand why she did it.

723
00:40:44,440 --> 00:40:49,280
She did it for someone
she really cared about

724
00:40:50,160 --> 00:40:52,320
and wanted to help someone fulfill a wish.

725
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,560
That's why she sacrificed herself.

726
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:56,640
Just like you did it for Ben,

727
00:40:56,760 --> 00:40:59,840
and took such good care of me.

728
00:41:00,040 --> 00:41:02,160
Just like you did it for Ben,

729
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:05,040
you're determined to get well.

730
00:41:06,880 --> 00:41:09,840
I'm determined, but I'm doing it for you.

731
00:41:09,920 --> 00:41:11,840
I don't want to become such a burden.

732
00:41:11,920 --> 00:41:14,640
Besides, I promised you I will try hard.

733
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:19,840
Your seasonal drink, hot pumpkin latte.

734
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:21,280
Thanks.

735
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:22,680
Thank you.

736
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:46,000
It tastes better with cardamom powder.

737
00:41:46,080 --> 00:41:47,160
Try it.

738
00:41:49,680 --> 00:41:50,400
See?

739
00:41:51,160 --> 00:41:52,400
You're right.

740
00:41:56,360 --> 00:41:57,040
Try it.

741
00:42:06,720 --> 00:42:07,360
Thank you.

742
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:22,000
We should come here often for coffee.

743
00:42:22,160 --> 00:42:25,040
And try all their seasonal drinks.
